{\b\fs40 Film 18: What do cold showers really do?}\par\par
Posts 2026-11-28. Read each line twice, in your own voice: savage, direct, funny. Leave three seconds of silence after each take. One audio file for the whole film, into folder 3 Your recordings.\par\par
{\b Line 1}\par You scream through a cold shower every morning because a podcast promised it would fix your whole life. Let's see what it does.\par\par
{\b Line 2}\par In the biggest trial, Dutch adults ended their shower with thirty to ninety seconds of cold water every day for a month.\par\par
{\b Line 3}\par They reported about thirty percent fewer days off sick, but no fewer days feeling ill. They still felt ill, but they went to more meetings.\par\par
{\b Line 4}\par But across eleven trials, mostly of ice baths, there was no proof that cold water boosts immunity or mood.\par\par
{\b Line 5}\par If you lift weights, skip the ice bath straight after training, because in trials it may blunt muscle growth.\par\par
{\b Line 6}\par And for fat loss, one small trial found people lost about seven hundred grams of fat in six weeks, from two hours a day at seventeen degrees Celsius. I hope your showers are shorter.\par\par
{\b Line 7}\par Plunging into cold water triggers a gasp and a racing heart in the first minute, and that shock can cause heart attacks, even in fairly young, healthy people. So if you have a heart condition, high blood pressure, diabetes or poor circulation, or you're pregnant, talk to your doctor before you start.\par\par
{\b Line 8}\par Let's get you back to factory settings.\par\par
